Explanation of the change:

1. We’ve located the `if (typeof itemRender === 'function')` branch inside `getPictureCardList`.
2. Instead of dropping all the default controls when the user provides `itemRender`, we now:
   - Call their `itemRender(file)` into a `customItem` node.
   - Wrap it together with our standard “ashbin” `<Icon>` (delete) if `closable` is true and we’re not in preview.
3. Default behavior (the `else` branch) remains exactly as before.

With this in place, supplying a custom `itemRender` will still render the delete icon and wire it up to `onClose`, restoring the missing remove functionality.
